# Binaries
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
bin/
build/
dist/
# goreleaser SBOM before-hook output (regenerated each build; embedded in archives)
gograph.cdx.json

# Test and coverage artefacts
*.test
*.out
*.prof
*.testlog
coverage.txt
coverage.html
# Per-invocation coverage temporaries (scripts/cover_gate.sh, rmp #2268). The
# script removes these on exit; the patterns cover a run killed before its trap.
cover.out.*
cover.lib.out.*

# pprof profiles
cpu.pprof
mem.pprof
*.pprof

# Benchmarks
benchstat.txt
*.bench

# Editor and OS detritus
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# Go workspace
go.work
go.work.sum

# Local environment
.env
.envrc

# Generated documentation
docs/_site/

# Compiled example binaries (matching examples/<NN>_*)
[0-9][0-9]_*
!examples/[0-9][0-9]_*/

# Soak-harness artefacts and stray go-run binary.
# The /-anchored entries catch the top-level directory; the un-anchored
# pattern catches the same name in subdirectories (e.g. when 'go test'
# is invoked from bench/soak/, the artefacts land in
# bench/soak/soak-artefacts/).
/soak
/soak-artefacts/
soak-artefacts/

# Local Claude Code session data and build artifacts
.claude/
# Anchor at the repo root so the pattern matches only the compiled
# binary, not the cmd/crashinject-helper/ directory containing main.go.
/crashinject-helper

# pgregory.net/rapid writes a reproduction file under testdata/rapid/<Test>/ when a
# property FAILS. Those are transient debugging artefacts of a failing run — twice
# now one has been committed after a deliberate mutation test, recording a
# reproduction for a defect that does not exist. Rapid replays any failfile it finds,
# so a stale one is noise at best. Genuine regressions belong in an explicit test
# case, not in a replay file.
# The leading **/ is load-bearing: a pattern with a slash anywhere but the end is
# anchored to THIS file's directory, so a bare `testdata/rapid/` matched only a
# top-level one and never cypher/testdata/rapid/ — which is why the artefacts kept
# arriving despite the rule.
**/testdata/rapid/
